From: Tam Do <tam.do@manyhobbies.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: sunxi-mmc: reset the controller after an update-clock timeout

When the clock-update command (UPCLK_ONLY | WAIT_PRE_OVER) times out,
it is left pending in the controller. Every later clock update by the
core's retries then times out too, so the card is never initialised for
the rest of the boot, even once the condition that blocked the first
command is gone.

On a board whose SDIO Wi-Fi rails come up just after the controller
starts probing, the card holds DAT0 busy for a moment and the first
update times out on about half of all boots. Re-initialising the
controller at the timeout (reset plus the init_host register setup)
lets the next retry succeed.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Tam Do <tam.do@manyhobbies.com>
---
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c
@@ -689,6 +689,12 @@
 
 	if (rval & SDXC_START) {
 		dev_err(mmc_dev(host->mmc), "fatal err update clk timeout\n");
+		/*
+		 * The command stays pending (e.g. on a card holding DAT0 busy
+		 * while it powers up) and would time out every retry: reset the
+		 * controller so the core's next attempt starts clean.
+		 */
+		sunxi_mmc_init_host(host);
 		return -EIO;
 	}
 
